===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leyg-|id=like}}
Verb from {{inh|en|enm|liken}}, from {{inh|en|ang|līcian||to like, to please}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*līkēn}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*līkāną}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*leyg-||image; likeness; similarity}}.

Cognate with {{cog|stq|liekje||to be similar, resemble}}, {{cog|fy|lykje||to seem, appear, look}}, {{cog|nl|lijken||to seem}}, {{cog|nds|lieken||to be like; resemble}}, {{cog|de|gleichen||to resemble}}, {{cog|sv|lika||to like; put up with; align with}}, {{cog|no|like||to like}}, {{cog|is|-}} and {{cog|fo|líka||to like}}.

Noun from {{inh|en|enm|like|t=pleasure, will, like}}, from the verb {{der|en|enm|liken|t=to like}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{sid|en|enjoy}} To [[enjoy]], be pleased by; [[favor]]; be in favor of.
#: {{ant|en|dislike|hate|mislike|disapprove}}
