##* {{quote-book|en|author=Sir {{w|Philip Sidney}}| passage=I willingly confess that it '''likes''' me much better when I find virtue in a fair lodging than when I am bound to seek it in an ill-favoured creature.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=7ZpMAAAAcAAJ&pg=RA1-PA83&dq=dunghill.&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwinxIyUndDiAhWwmeAKHXD6BmQQ6AEINTAC#v=onepage&q=dunghill.&f=false| title=The Countess of Pembroke's Arcadia|year=16th century}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1608|author=w:William Shakespeare| title=w:King Lear| section=act 2, scene 2| passage=His countenance '''likes''' me not.}}
